ow routes on-demand pages to `_middleware` instead of `_isr` when a middleware entry point exists, and the generated edge middleware forwards `next()` to `/_isr?x_astro_path=…&x_astro_path_token=…` for ISR-backed routes and to `/_render` otherwise. This is covered by the new `isr-with-edge-middleware` fixture and its assertions on both `config.json` route `dest`s and the runtime forwarding logic of the built `middleware.mjs`.\n- **Preserve ISR behavior for `isr.exclude`, internal endpoints, and prerendered pages** — `isr.exclude` paths are added to the middleware’s excluded-pattern list (checked first) and still forwarded to `/_render`. `_image` and `_server-islands` continue to bypass middleware and go straight to `_render`. Prerendered pages receive no route entry and are served as static files, as asserted by the tests.\n- **Fix query-string loss when middleware forwards a request** — `serverless/entrypoint.ts` now parses the trusted `x-astro-path` header with `URL` so the query string is preserved instead of being encoded into the pathname. The new tests cover query preservation for both middleware-header and route-rewrite paths.\n- **Keep routing unchanged when there is no middleware file** — The `isr-edge-no-middleware` fixture asserts that routes still point directly at `/_isr` and no `_middleware.func` is built.\n- **Changeset** — `.changeset/isr-edge-middleware.md` is present and correctly scoped as a `@astrojs/vercel` patch.\n\n## Questions\n\n- Several tests in `packages/integrations/vercel/test/isr-edge-middleware.test.ts` replace and restore `globalThis.fetch`. If `astro-scripts test` runs tests concurrently (the `node:test` default), those stubs could leak between concurrent tests and produce flaky failures. Is the test harness configured to run this file serially?\n\n## Review Status\n\nVerdict: ready to merge based on static review\nContext: PR #17687 plus its description\nScope: Full PR diff (base `e28d22782bdc641261d0eca8ad00ba248a93d640`, head `bf